# The first step is the start of the guide: its Next plays it, so it waits for nothing.
step The approved link
  look Mail: Marcus's message, and the link under it
  move Click the link under Marcus's message.
  | Recording 4 of 5 is next. Marcus in IT has sent the link to the converter the company approved. This round is the normal one, so you know what a normal install looks like.
  | The email links to software.northwind.example, the company's own portal. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-convert

step Sign in to the company portal
  look the two boxes: Username and Password
  when visit portal-convert
  cue field:portal-login:0 field:portal-login:1 choice:portal-login-1 choice:portal-convert-1 app:browser
  move Copy the details from portal-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”. Then click “Install”.
  | The portal asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: Username and Password. Remember what a normal page and a normal installer look like.
open portal-convert

step Sign in, and install the approved tool
  look the portal's “Download started” page, and the file in Downloads
  when choose portal-convert 1
  move Double-click northwind-convert-setup.exe in Downloads.
  | You are in. The portal said who made the tool and what else comes with it: nothing. The installer is saved to Downloads. Nothing has run yet.
signin portal-login
choose portal-convert 1
file Downloads/northwind-convert-setup.exe
  program ncsetup
  size 2097152
open Downloads

step Your computer checks the installer
  look {the Open File - Security Warning: Publisher “Northwind Traders IT”, Type “Application”, then the permission prompt|the warning: “northwind-convert-setup.exe” is a Windows program, then the password prompt}
  when prompt ncsetup
  cue dialog-btn:run dialog-btn:ok view-btn:next view-btn:done view:nc-setup
  move {Click Run, then Yes.|In the warning, click “Show what it does”, then OK.}
  | {Windows asks before a downloaded program runs. The publisher is the company's own and the file is signed.|The Mac warns that this is a Windows program: the training desktop shows what it did on the PC it was made for.}
open Downloads/northwind-convert-setup.exe

step The setup opens
  look the setup window: two pages, and nothing offered but the tool
  when run ncsetup
  cue view-btn:next view-btn:done view:nc-setup
  move Click Next, then Finish.
  | A plain setup: a welcome, then a done page, and nothing offered but the tool. No offers, no ticked boxes. This is what a plain installer looks like.
answer run
answer run

step Recording 4 done
  look the counter in the guide: 4 of 5
  when done nc-setup
  cue choice:download-1 link:mail-wma mail:mail-wma app:mail
  move Open Priya’s email and click the link.
  | Recording 4 is converted: 4 of 5. One recording is left, and another email has just arrived.
press nc-setup next
press nc-setup done
quota +1

